  "step_3": "The decision reason requires preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, which would be Lottery B (25% > 20%). However, the individual chose Lottery A and justified this by stating the 5% difference in probability was too small to matter. This suggests they did not follow the rule of the decision reason; instead, they discounted the probability difference. While they did consider the probabilities (so there is some overlap in information use), they did not apply the rule of preferring the higher probability option. Their reasoning runs contrary to the decision reason’s rule. Therefore, it is clear they did not use this reason to make their decision.",
